    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d542">

                <pb facs="0444" n="432" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg432"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.515/61: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wharton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-10T13:00:00-00:44">March 10, 1942—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:38 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>66. From McBride. Legation’s 62, March 8, 10 a.m. President Barclay is willing to
                    proceed with monetary reform immediately provided some general arrangement such
                    as suggested in No. 62 is found practicable by American officials.
                    [McBride.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wharton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
